; TEST: abort=1
;
; u40 (2^32 - 1)(2^32 + 1) = 2^64 - 1.
; Abort kind 1, the numeric trap (prelude/README.md) -- the shared
; `bfausr_trap`. If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; The complement of trap_mul_u40_2p64.ir: this product is just BELOW 2^64,
; so the 64-bit `mul` does not overflow and CF stays clear; what traps is the
; compare -- 2^64 - 1 normalised to 40 bits is 2^40 - 1, not itself. (Both
; u40 products trap: anything at or above 2^40 is out of range. The two
; fixtures differ in which check catches it.)
;
; Mutation (run): the compare dropped, the flag kept -> exit 7.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u40 4294967295
%2 = iconst u40 4294967297
%3 = mul u40 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
